#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0562 expect=violation domain=VS
#note "D1 (runbook W6, owner 2026-09-28: record_count's regex= is IMPLEMENTED, with is_unique_set's semantics): two SYSBP records on the SAME DATE at different times (2014-01-01T08:00 and T09:00) with the same VSREPNUM. The binding's regex ^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2} collapses VSDTC to its date before grouping, so the timing group holds 2 records, and the Check's is_unique_set (the same regex) finds the two VSREPNUM = 1 duplicates within it -> both rows fire. RED on the pre-port engine (measured W6 phase 0): the operation declared regex= and never read it, so it counted 1 per full datetime while the Check already grouped by date, and the two halves disagreed silently."
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015 VSSEQ=1
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=01-701-1015 VSSEQ=2
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#library domain-variables VS USUBJID:Identifier VSTESTCD:Topic VSDTC:Timing VSREPNUM:Qualifier DOMAIN:Identifier
dataset VS label="Vital Signs"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VSSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col VSTESTCD type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Short Name"
col VSDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of Measurements"
col VSREPNUM type=Char label="Repetition Number"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | VS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | SYSBP | 2014-01-01T08:00 | 1
CDISCPILOT01 | VS | 01-701-1015 | 2 | SYSBP | 2014-01-01T09:00 | 1
---
